          "When you sit in front of an office computer staring at a blank document, career confusion often creeps in. At this point, many people get stuck between two opposing options: pursuing a high-paying job or discovering their true passion. When tackling this dilemma, the most essential step is to lay the costs of both options on the table for comparison. Clarifying your minimum monthly financial expenses and psychological tolerance can effectively reduce the helplessness caused by the unknown.",
          "If you fall into a dilemma, you might mistakenly assume that choosing one path means completely losing the benefits of the other. This black-and-white thinking pattern makes people even more hesitant to submit job applications. Instead, you should focus on building a buffer period rather than forcing yourself to make an immediate, major, and irreversible career transition.",
